33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '## Motivation\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'Instead of implementing `XMLHttpRequest` in Node.js to run browser-specific [Fetch polyfill](https://github.com/github/fetch), why not go from native `http` to `fetch` API directly? Hence, `node-fetch`, minimal code for a `window.fetch` compatible API on Node.js runtime.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "See Matt Andrews' [isomorphic-fetch](https://github.com/matthew-andrews/isomorphic-fetch) or Leonardo Quixada's [cross-fetch](https://github.com/lquixada/cross-fetch) for isomorphic usage (exports `node-fetch` for server-side, `whatwg-fetch` for client-side).\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '## Features\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- Stay consistent with `window.fetch` API.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- Make conscious trade-off when following [WHATWG fetch spec][whatwg-fetch] and [stream spec](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/) implementation details, document known differences.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- Use native promise but allow substituting it with [insert your favorite promise library].\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- Use native Node streams for body on both request and response.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- Decode content encoding (gzip/deflate) properly and convert string output (such as `res.text()` and `res.json()`) to UTF-8 automatically.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- Useful extensions such as timeout, redirect limit, response size limit, [explicit errors](ERROR-HANDLING.md) for troubleshooting.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '## Difference from client-side fetch\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- See [Known Differences](LIMITS.md) for details.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- If you happen to use a missing feature that `window.fetch` offers, feel free to open an issue.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '- Pull requests are welcomed too!\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '## Installation\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'Current stable release (`2.x`)\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```sh\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '$ npm install node-fetch\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '## Loading and configuring the module\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'We suggest you load the module via `require` until the stabilization of ES modules in node:\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "const fetch = require('node-fetch');\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'If you are using a Promise library other than native, set it through `fetch.Promise`:\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "const Bluebird = require('bluebird');\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'fetch.Promise = Bluebird;\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '## Common Usage\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'NOTE: The documentation below is up-to-date with `2.x` releases; see the [`1.x` readme](https://github.com/bitinn/node-fetch/blob/1.x/README.md), [changelog](https://github.com/bitinn/node-fetch/blob/1.x/CHANGELOG.md) and [2.x upgrade guide](UPGRADE-GUIDE.md) for the differences.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '#### Plain text or HTML\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://github.com/')\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.text())\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(body => console.log(body));\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '#### JSON\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://api.github.com/users/github')\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.json())\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(json => console.log(json));\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '#### Simple Post\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://httpbin.org/post', { method: 'POST', body: 'a=1' })\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.json()) // expecting a json response\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(json => console.log(json));\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '#### Post with JSON\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'const body = { a: 1 };\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://httpbin.org/post', {\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       "        method: 'post',\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '        body:    JSON.stringify(body),\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '    })\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.json())\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(json => console.log(json));\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '#### Post with form parameters\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '`URLSearchParams` is available in Node.js as of v7.5.0. See [official documentation](https://nodejs.org/api/url.html#url_class_urlsearchparams) for more usage methods.\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'NOTE: The `Content-Type` header is only set automatically to `x-www-form-urlencoded` when an instance of `URLSearchParams` is given as such:\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "const { URLSearchParams } = require('url');\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       'const params = new URLSearchParams();\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "params.append('a', 1);\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://httpbin.org/post', { method: 'POST', body: params })\n" +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.json())\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '    .then(json => console.log(json));\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '\n' +
33121 silly install resolved       '#### Handling exceptions\n' +
